# Security headers for the Milez Ahead booking site (Cloudflare Pages).
# Security audit 2026-09-14 (M9 + L3).
#
# Deliberately a SAFE subset: clickjacking + base-tag + plugin lockdown, and a
# referrer policy that never leaks a full URL (with a tracking token) cross-site.
# We do NOT set a strict script-src/connect-src CSP here — the booking pages carry
# inline scripts and call several external origins (Google Maps/Places, Paystack,
# Supabase), so an untested enforcing CSP could break the live booking form. A full
# CSP is a follow-up: roll out Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only first, confirm no
# violations across every page, then promote to enforcing.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'
